From 810ffb2efc51d26b5e3db41f078952b3930d0dda Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brhett <36874370+jingledingle521@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 22:52:37 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 41/45] Finder: use the system accent color instead of macOS
 blue

finderAccent() reads the accent picked in System Settings from
kdeglobals ([General] AccentColor). The palette only carries KDE's darker
selection shade. The accent is read again whenever the palette changes,
so switching it takes effect without a restart. Selections, AirDrop,
transfer cards and the file chooser's default button use it; the
sidebar follows in the next commit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
